  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool/transformer) achieves ~0.65 acc, while image-only with resnet50 is near chance (0.208). The critical unanswered question is whether fusing the weak image signal with the strong RNA signal via concat fusion yields any benefit over the RNA-only baseline. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is a clean, single-variable comparison against config_005 (RNA-only, same encoder/profile/aggregation, acc=0.650): the only added factor is the image branch and concat fusion. If accuracy stays near or below 0.65, it strongly suggests the image modality (with resnet50) adds no value and budget should focus on RNA-only refinement. If it improves, it justifies further exploration of fusion strategies and image encoders. This is the most informative next step because it directly resolves the central multimodality question before committing budget to more complex fusion or image-encoder variants."
}

